natural_abilities:
  - name: "Impervious to Cold"
    description: "Sub-zero temperatures do the psychic no harm: no exposure, frostbite or hypothermia, even unclothed in the worst weather, and icy water or soaked clothes impose no penalty. Handles ice, frozen metal and even liquid nitrogen unharmed and only starts to feel chilly far below zero. Magical or Mega-Damage cold attacks do just 10% of normal damage. Snow, rain, fog and snow glare still hamper vision as usual."
  - name: "Clairvoyant Weather Trance (Sense Storms)"
    description: "After a meditative trance of 2D6 minutes, foresees the weather and storms headed for a 20 mile (32 km) radius, one day ahead per level (24 hours at level 1, four days at level 4). For winter weather the forecast is exact to the minute: arrival time, direction, path, speed, size, duration and intensity, the kind of precipitation, snowfall depth, wind and blizzard conditions, visibility, fog and sudden temperature swings that bring frostbite, ice, thaw or flooding. Rain, thunderstorms, tornados, hurricanes and fog are foreseen too, but only to within 2D4x10 minutes. Cannot foresee wind or dust storms, lightning alone, a dry Ley Line Storm, or magically made weather, though he recognizes an unnatural storm once it arrives. Inside any storm he never loses his sense of direction and can tell its speed, heading and whether it will soon pass; the full timetable still needs the trance. I.S.P.: 4."
  - name: "Sense Cold Weather Danger"
    description: "Senses present or developing winter and water hazards and the direction they lie in, though not their exact spot: thin ice, snow pits, weak ice bridges, icy roads, avalanche conditions, deep snow (halve Spd) or ice (Spd -80%), a sharp temperature drop, icebergs or ice flows, thaw or storm flooding, mudslides, fog and a storm due within the hour. Range: 300 foot (91.4 m) radius per level. Duration: 10 minutes +1 minute per level. I.S.P.: 2."
  - name: "Reduce Atmospheric Temperature"
    description: "Chills a room, vehicle or small area by 10 degrees F (5.6 C) a minute, down to 0 F (-18 C), and keeps it there. Hard on anyone without environmental armor; given time, water and most liquids freeze, and electronics not built for outdoor cold may glitch or quit after half an hour. Radius: 10 feet (3 m) per level. Duration: 15 minutes, extended 15 minutes at a time for another 4 I.S.P., but only while he stays and concentrates, which halves his melee attacks or actions and gives -30% on skills. I.S.P.: 4 per 15 minutes."
  - name: "Freeze Water/Liquids"
    description: "Freezes one gallon (3.8 liters) per level, by touch or by sight, solid within one melee round (15 seconds); he must see the liquid or know it is in range. No effect on living creatures, oil, gasoline, kerosene, strong alcohol such as vodka, or anything holding antifreeze. Range: touch or 8 feet (2.4 m) +2 feet (0.6 m) per level. Duration: stays frozen until it is warm enough to thaw. I.S.P.: 4."
  - name: "Frost or Ice"
    description: "Coats surfaces with frost, three square feet (0.28 sq. m) per level in one patch or spread over several. Frosted glass, screens and visors cut visibility by 80%: shapes and lights only, with -50% to piloting and -5 to strike, parry or dodge for a moving vehicle or a visored wearer. Frost on a floor makes people slip on a D20 roll of 1-15, losing two melee attacks with a 55% chance to drop what they hold. Range: touch or 15 feet (4.6 m). Duration: until scraped off in freezing weather, or melted by heat or flame; at 38-50 F (3.3-10 C) it lasts 1D4 minutes, in warmer air 1D4 melee rounds. I.S.P.: 3. Making a thin ice sheet rather than frost doubles both cost and duration."
  - name: "Ice Shards (S.D.C.)"
    description: "Conjures two finger-sized ice spikes, both in one hand or one in each, to throw together (one attack) or one after the other (two attacks), +1 to strike on top of other bonuses. Damage: 1D6 S.D.C. per shard. Not a melee weapon. Range: 60 feet (18.3 m) thrown. They last only a few seconds and must be thrown in the round they appear. I.S.P.: 3. Alternatively, for one full melee round he may throw existing icicles or chunks of ice, one or two per attack, with the same damage, bonus and range whatever their shape."
  - name: "Ice Blades (M.D.C.)"
    description: "Conjures a knife-sized ice dagger in each hand, used singly or as a pair to strike and parry, +1 to strike on top of attribute, combat and W.P. bonuses. Either may be thrown (both together is one attack, one after the other two attacks), range 60 feet (18.3 m). Damage: 1 M.D. per blade against physical M.D.C. foes (2D6 S.D.C. against S.D.C. targets or in S.D.C. settings); 1D6 M.D. per blade against Entities, spirits, ghosts, energy and Astral Beings, and vampires in solid form (not in mist form). They last 15 seconds (one melee round) per level, then melt to water. I.S.P.: 6. Ice Claw option: the blades jut from the four fingertips as claws, cannot be thrown, and give -30% to skills needing a deft touch such as Art, Computer Operation, Forgery, Pick Locks or Pick Pockets. Ice Sword option: one slender three foot (0.9 m) blade doing 1D4 M.D. (2D6+2 S.D.C.), same cost, bonus and duration, -3 to strike if thrown."
  - name: "Ice Armor (Super-Psionic)"
    description: "Covers the body in plates of ice, either selected spots or a full suit, worn over armor, clothes or bare skin. Bulky: Spd -40% and -20% to mobility skills such as Acrobatics, Climb and Prowl, but not Swimming (the ice floats), and no loss of attacks per melee. Armor: 15 M.D.C. per level (or 24 S.D.C. where S.D.C. rules apply). Self only. Duration: five minutes per level, or until destroyed. I.S.P.: 10."
  - name: "Calm Snowstorm (Super-Psionic)"
    description: "Four or more Cold Born standing or sitting outdoors in a snow or ice storm, hands joined and concentrating, cut its intensity, wind and accumulation by 3% for each participant, keeping a pocket of relative calm in a blizzard. Range: 300 foot (91.4 m) radius per participant, whatever their level. Duration: as long as all of them stay outside and keep focusing. I.S.P.: 10 per Cold Born per hour."
  - name: "Master Psychic"
    description: "I.S.P.: 3D4x10 plus the M.E. attribute, +10 per additional level. Regains I.S.P. at 2 an hour while sleeping, 12 an hour while meditating. As a Master Psychic, saves vs psionic attack on a 10 or higher. Powers 2-10 above are exclusive to the Cold Born. One more power from the Cold Born list at levels 2, 3, 5, 6, 7, 9, 11, 13 and 15; Hydrokinesis counts as two selections."
  - name: "Cold-Weather Instincts"
    description: "Perception +3 in winter matters: cold weather, snow and ice, judging whether snow or ice will hold, and noticing traps or hidden hazards in winter terrain. Strike and parry +1, but only when using ice attacks or psionics. Neither is added to the sheet."
